From 323377a1907f6c300c1e29543e26f8f390b4092d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jabern <Jabern@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:10:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] ntdll, nsiproxy: Describe the machine and its network
 when Android hides them.

Android apps get no DMI (/sys/class/dmi/id), no dbus machine-id, no
SIOCGIFHWADDR, no netlink (if_nameindex, getifaddrs) and no /proc/net. Rhino's
licensing then failed with a NullReferenceException (empty UUID/serials/MAC).

- ntdll: DMI files and the machine-id fall back to $WINE_DMI_DIR/<name>.
- nsiproxy: stable locally administered MAC (machine-id + interface name) when
  SIOCGIFHWADDR is denied; interfaces and IPv4 addresses from SIOCGIFCONF when
  netlink is denied; an unreadable /proc/net/route reads as empty.

All fallbacks only run when the normal Linux call fails with EACCES/EPERM or
the file is missing, so regular Linux builds behave as before.
